 "notes": "30 stations, lines 3315-3344, all in a single column under the sub-heading 'Nos. and Names of Stations.' (line 3313). This list has no keepers, marks or light characters. It only gives the numbers and names used to read the day grid (lines 3346-3414). Fragments leave out the leading indentation. 'coast' is 'Irish Coast', taken from the section heading 'IRISH COAST: AUTUMN.'. The list itself has no coast sub-headings.\n\nChoices a reader should know about:\n- '6. Barrels Rock, do.' and '10. Kirk Bank, do.': 'do.' (ditto) stands for 'Lt.-ship' from the rows above. I put 'do.' in type as printed rather than expanding it. The comma before 'do.' stays at the end of the name ('Barrels Rock,', 'Kirk Bank,').\n- '8. Arklow S. Lt.-ship.': the type is given as 'Lt.-ship.' with its trailing full stop, as printed. Row 5 has 'Lt.-ship' without one.\n- '3. Old Head, Kinsale': I split this as name 'Old Head' and place 'Kinsale', like 'Calf Rock, Cork' on line 3307. The lighthouse is usually called 'Old Head of Kinsale', so you could keep the whole string as the name instead.\n- '27. Black Rock (Mayo)': name 'Black Rock', place 'Mayo'. The brackets are left out of the place but kept in the fragment.\n- The N./S./E./W. suffixes ('Oyster Island N.', 'Eagle Island E.' and so on) are part of the station names and stay in name.\n\nPrinted spellings kept as they are: 'Kirk Bank' is surely Kish Bank. 'Howth Baily' is usually spelled Bailey. 'Innishtrahull' is printed with a double n. 'Arran Island N./S.' are the Aran Islands, Galway.\n\nGaps in the numbering: 9, 14, 18, 22, 28, 33, 35, 36, 37 and 40 are not listed. These were presumably stations that sent no dated entries this autumn. Number 40, Calf Rock, Cork, is marked 'Destroyed in storm, Nov. 1881' on line 3307 just above.\n\nOutside these lines, from the part of the grid I looked at: on line 3351 (3rd September) the grid lists station '82'. No such station exists, so it is probably a misprint for 32 (Arran Island N.). I only looked at grid lines 3346-3355, not the whole grid.",
